.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Graphify "Hive Mind" -----------------------------------------------
# graphify-out/ is INTENTIONALLY NOT ignored wholesale: graph.json,
# GRAPH_REPORT.md, graph.html, and obsidian/ are the shared team graph and
# MUST be committed so every teammate gets the same knowledge graph via git.
#
# Only the machine-local/regenerable build state is ignored below:
#   - .graphify_*.json / .graphify_python / .graphify_root: internal pipeline
#     intermediates (AST/semantic/chunk dumps) and an ABSOLUTE, per-machine
#     Python interpreter path — committing .graphify_python would point
#     teammates at your local venv path.
#   - cache/: regenerable AST/semantic extraction cache (rebuilt automatically).
#   - cost.json: local LLM token/cost usage log, not project knowledge.
#   - manifest.json: per-file mtime/hash tracking used only for incremental
#     `--update` detection; timestamps are absolute and machine-specific, so
#     committing it just churns on every clone/commit with no shared value.
# See README.md "Updating the Hive Mind" for how graph.json/GRAPH_REPORT.md/
# obsidian/ get regenerated and re-committed.
graphify-out/.graphify_*
graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/cost.json
graphify-out/manifest.json

# Claude Code — personal/local permission overrides, not shared project config
# (.claude/settings.json and .claude/skills/ ARE committed — see README.md)
.claude/settings.local.json

# MCP server registration files can embed an absolute, machine-specific
# interpreter path (see README.md "Registering the Graphify MCP server")
.mcp.json
